the white house is again blasting  republican governors who are  transporting asylum seekers to  democratic-led cities  florida governor ron desantis has  promised to exhaust a 12 million dollar  state-funded program to bring more  migrants to other states this comes just  days after desantis sent two planes  carrying nearly 50 migrants to martha's  vineyard massachusetts they were moved  to a temporary shelter at joint base  cape cod and elaine quijano is there  with more elaine good morning  good morning to you jeff well one of the  lawyers who accompanied the migrants  from martha's vineyard told us that some  of them were reluctant to leave the  island after what they experienced  during that initial trip to  massachusetts for these migrants coming  here to a u.s military base represents  yet another step on an uncertain journey  it was an emotional send-off from  volunteers as 48 migrants who landed on  martha's vineyard wednesday left a  church shelter hola  in my heart  the asylum seekers voluntarily continued  their trek off the island by ferry where  we met 28 year old eliezer perche who  came from venezuela with his parents  says he's hoping to find some work and a  better life for his family  they'll temporarily live dormitory style  at a military base on cape cod which has  been set up as an emergency shelter all  organized by massachusetts republican  governor charlie baker  president biden criticized the  republican governors of florida texas  and arizona who've sent nearly 12 000  migrants to democratic strongholds in  the past five months instead of working  with us on solutions republicans are  playing politics with human beings using  them as props  what they're doing is simply wrong it's  unamerican it's reckless  florida republican governor ron desantis  who organized the migrant flights from  texas to martha's vineyard using a 12  million dollar fund defended his actions  they already bust them out they're gone  they said they said we want everyone no  one's illegal and they're gone within 48  hours  here on cape cod it's not clear just how  long the migrants will stay on this  military base massachusetts state  agencies are working with non-profit  groups to ensure the migrants have  access to a wide variety of services  including legal assistance and health  care dana  all right elaine thank you
 

